  "text_md": "## EXAMPLES\n\nON THE\n\n## INTEGRAL CALCULUS.\n\n## CHAPTER I.\n\nELEMENTARY INTEGRALS TO BE COMMITTED TO MEMORY.\n\n$$(1.) \\int \\frac{dx}{x} = \\log x.$$\n\n(2.) \n$$\\int \\frac{dx}{a+bx^2} = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{ab}} \\tan^{-1}\\left(x\\sqrt{\\frac{b}{a}}\\right), \\text{ or } \\int \\frac{dx}{a^2+x^2}$$\n$$= \\frac{1}{a} \\tan^{-1} \\frac{x}{a}.$$\n\n$$(3.) \\int \\frac{dx}{\\sqrt{a^2 - x^2}} = \\sin^{-1} \\frac{x}{a}.$$\n\n$$(4.) \\int \\frac{-dx}{\\sqrt{a^2 - x^2}} = \\cos^{-1} \\frac{x}{a}.$$\n\n$$(5.) \\int \\frac{dx}{\\sqrt{x^2 \\pm a^2}} = \\log \\frac{(x + \\sqrt{x^2 \\pm a^2})}{a}.$$\n\n(6.) \n$$\\int \\frac{dx}{\\sqrt{2} a x - x^2} = \\text{vers}^{-1} \\frac{x}{a}.$$\n\n(7.) \n$$\\int \\frac{dx}{\\sqrt{x^2 + 2 ax}} = \\log(x \\pm a + \\sqrt{x^2 \\pm 2 ax})$$\n\n(8.) \n$$\\int \\frac{dx}{x\\sqrt{x^2-a^2}} = \\frac{1}{a}\\sec^{-1}\\frac{x}{a}.$$",
